<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qinghai Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kokonor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qinghai Lake, also known by its Mongolian name Kokonor, is the largest lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, a salt lake on the north-eastern Tibetan Plateau. Its grasslands supported pastoral peoples for millennia, and from the 4th to the 7th century they were the heartland of the Tuyuhun kingdom, which controlled routes between China, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qinghai-lake.jpg" alt="Qinghai Lake" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qinghai_lake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
